source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: Both tokens of a heading line break; a JFM ATX heading carries no hard break, so jiro keeps all four backslashes as heading text and warns once per forced newline.
-- input.jira --
h1. a\\b c\\d
-- rendered.html --
<h1><a name="a%5C%5Cbc%5C%5Cd"></a>a<br class="atl-forced-newline" />b c<br class="atl-forced-newline" />d</h1>
-- want.md --
# a\\\\b c\\\\d
-- warnings.json --
[
  {
    "Line": 1,
    "Column": 6,
    "Construct": "heading",
    "Reason": "Jira would render a forced newline inside this heading; a JFM heading cannot carry one, so the characters stay literal"
  },
  {
    "Line": 1,
    "Column": 11,
    "Construct": "heading",
    "Reason": "Jira would render a forced newline inside this heading; a JFM heading cannot carry one, so the characters stay literal"
  }
]
